From a61dfa7647e095a2cef15d4ad58f1e06c8222b92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrmaxmeier <3913977+Mrmaxmeier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:08:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix panic on grayscale non-XYB VarDCT frames (#908)

For a grayscale, non-XYB VarDCT frame the pipeline has no stage that consumes
colour channels 1 and 2: there is no XybStage, no YcbcrToRgbStage, and the save
stage only reads channel 0. The builder therefore prunes those channels and
leaves their `ChannelInfo::ty` as `None`. VarDCT nevertheless decodes all three
colour channels and asks the pipeline for a scratch buffer for each, so
`group_size_for_channel` panicked on `ty.unwrap()`.

The buffer size does not depend on the channel type; `ty` was only used to
assert that the caller and the pipeline agree. Run that check only when the
channel actually has a type, so unused channels get a correctly sized throwaway
buffer that `set_buffer_for_group` (already guarded by `channel_is_used`) drops.
This matches libjxl, which likewise decodes three channels and discards the two
it does not output.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Local backport scope: production changes only. Upstream regression tests,
fixtures, and test-only harness changes are intentionally omitted. The
original commit message above describes the full upstream change.

diff --git a/jxl/src/render/internal.rs b/jxl/src/render/internal.rs
index 57f0885ed..f6e2c4dc4 100644
--- a/jxl/src/render/internal.rs
+++ b/jxl/src/render/internal.rs
@@ -147,10 +147,15 @@ impl<Buffer> RenderPipelineShared<Buffer> {
         requested_data_type: DataTypeTag,
     ) -> (usize, usize) {
         let ChannelInfo { downsample, ty } = self.channel_info[0][channel];
-        if ty.unwrap() != requested_data_type {
+        // Channels that no stage consumes have no type at all. Callers may still ask for a
+        // scratch buffer for them (e.g. VarDCT always decodes three colour channels, but a
+        // grayscale pipeline only ever reads the first one); the data written there is
+        // discarded, so any type is acceptable.
+        if let Some(ty) = ty
+            && ty != requested_data_type
+        {
             panic!(
-                "Invalid pipeline usage: incorrect channel type, requested {:?}, but pipeline wants {ty:?}",
-                requested_data_type
+                "Invalid pipeline usage: incorrect channel type, requested {requested_data_type:?}, but pipeline wants {ty:?}"
             );
         }
         // 420 JPEGs are padded to 16 pixels, not to 8.
